 ## Overview
-Conditional Radiance Field Editing modifies a trained conditional radiance field to alter its appearance or geometry without retraining the entire model from scratch. It solves the problem of efficient, targeted scene manipulation by freezing the coarse network and optimizing only the fine network's parameters and associated latent codes. Unlike [Hybrid Updates for Editing](15974-hybrid-updates-for-editing.md), which may involve more complex update strategies, this method relies on a strict separation of coarse and fine networks to isolate the editing domain.
+Conditional Radiance Field Editing modifies a trained conditional radiance field by freezing the coarse network and optimizing only the fine network $F_{fine}$ and its associated latent codes [S1]. It solves the problem of efficient, targeted scene manipulation by requiring only 100 optimization iterations at a learning rate of $10^{-2}$ [S1].
 
