 ## Background
-The method originates from the work on Conditional Radiance Fields, specifically detailed in "Editing Conditional Radiance Fields" [S1]. It builds upon the original NeRF architecture [S1] and introduces a bottleneck for feature caching. The concept of editing via latent manipulation is further explored in "Unconstrained Scene Generation with Locally Conditioned Radiance Fields" [S2], which highlights the properties of local latent grids for scene synthesis.
